From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: senary MI2S for SM4450

The SM4450 boards (Retroid Pocket Classic, Anbernic RG 55G1) put their two
aw88166 speaker amps on the senary MI2S bus. Mainline 7.3's
sc8280xp_snd_hw_params() already covers SENARY: provider format on the CPU
DAI, and the per-DAI "bclk" (dai@93 under q6apmbedai) set and enabled
through the sm8450 card data. What SM4450 still needs on top:

- the codec format on every codec DAI of the link, not only the first,
  since both amps hang off it;
- the RP Classic's single-channel fixup;
- a bit clock that counts two I2S slots for that mono stream: mainline
  derives BCLK from the channel count, which would halve it to 768 kHz.
  The amps were proven at 1536000, the rate the card-level clock was
  pinned to before.

Our side of ROCKNIX SM4450 0030 ("add MI2S clock and format support").

retroforge, 7.3.1 bump: was a delta on our card-level "i2s_clk" startup
(0820/0825, both deleted for mainline's per-DAI MI2S clocks); now a delta
on mainline's hw_params alone.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
index d5859fb..a537663 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dapm.h>
 #include <sound/pcm.h>
@@ -101,8 +102,9 @@ static inline int sc8280xp_get_mclk_freq(struct snd_pcm_hw_params *params)
 
 static inline int sc8280xp_get_bclk_freq(struct snd_pcm_hw_params *params)
 {
+	/* An I2S frame carries two slots, even for a mono stream */
 	return I2S_BIT_RATE(params_rate(params),
-			    params_channels(params),
+			    max(params_channels(params), 2U),
 			    snd_pcm_format_width(params_format(params)));
 }
 
@@ -230,6 +232,18 @@ static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	channels->min = 2;
 	channels->max = 2;
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
+	case SENARY_MI2S_RX:
+		/*
+		 * The Retroid Pocket Classic drives both of its amps from one
+		 * channel. Everything else on this port is stereo, and forcing
+		 * mono there leaves the MFC and the I2S endpoint configured for
+		 * a single channel, so both amps reproduce the left one.
+		 */
+		if (!strcmp(rtd->card->name, "RetroidPocketClassic")) {
+			channels->min = 1;
+			channels->max = 1;
+		}
+		break;
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_1:
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_2:
@@ -253,7 +267,8 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	struct sc8280xp_snd_data *data = snd_soc_card_get_drvdata(rtd->card);
 	int mclk_freq = sc8280xp_get_mclk_freq(params);
 	int bclk_freq = sc8280xp_get_bclk_freq(params);
-	int ret;
+	struct snd_soc_dai *dai;
+	int i, ret;
 
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
 	case PRIMARY_MI2S_RX ... QUATERNARY_MI2S_TX:
@@ -265,10 +280,13 @@ static int sc8280xp_snd_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 			return ret;
 
 		if (data->priv->codec_dai_fmt) {
-			ret = snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(codec_dai,
-						  data->priv->codec_dai_fmt);
-			if (ret && ret != -ENOTSUPP)
-				return ret;
+			/* SM4450 boards hang two amps off one MI2S link */
+			for_each_rtd_codec_dais(rtd, i, dai) {
+				ret = snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(dai,
+							  data->priv->codec_dai_fmt);
+				if (ret && ret != -ENOTSUPP)
+					return ret;
+			}
 		}
 
 		if (data->priv->mi2s_mclk_enable) {
